# PSP ad hoc between nx-mobile devices on one Wi-Fi with nobody typing a server address: the frontend's runner
# (NX_ENVIRONMENT_SET_PSP_LINK, libretro/nx_psp_link.h) finds the other devices and chooses which one runs the ad hoc
# server. The core takes its server from the runner at each login, starts and stops its built-in server when told,
# logs in again when the server changes, and reports when the game enters ad hoc mode and joins or leaves a group.
# A game that only calls sceNetAdhocctlInit touches no network; the login waits for its first Scan / Create /
# Connect / Join. Every ad hoc socket (the server connection, PDP, PTP, accepted ones, the built-in server's) is
# routed onto the runner's network, and this device's address is the one on it. A lost server connection, a new
# server, the runner's leave and a login that finds no server each tell a game in a group or joining one that it is
# disconnected, and end a scan that can no longer be answered as one that found nothing; after a leave the device
# stays off the server until rejoin or, on the automatic route, until the game re-enters ad hoc; with nx_psp_link
# switched off it stays off, and a session turned into the automatic route comes back by that route's rule. The
# runner hears from the core when another device is on this device's server, even after the game left ad hoc, so it
# keeps that server.
# The core reports its presence, and refuses save states while in ad hoc. Without a frontend that answers the call,
# the core behaves as upstream.
